  "notes": "AgroGeneration S.A. (Euronext Growth Paris, ticker ALAGR). Identified via seed-comps and Boursorama lookup \u2014 NOT Agripower or Vilmorin. AgroGeneration operates ~28,500 ha (~70.4k acres) of Ukrainian farmland under long-term lease, growing wheat, sunflower, corn, and soy in Kharkiv region. French semi-annual reporter (H1 June + FY December). War-impacted since 2022 with Kharkiv operations near front lines; multiple write-downs. Tiny float (~100M shares); equity recapitalized 2023. Per-share NAV \u20ac0.111 per seed-comps. Coverage limited \u2014 only headline P&L disclosed in interim communiqu\u00e9s. AgroGeneration IPO'd on Alternext (now Euronext Growth) Paris in March 2010. Initially diversified with Argentinian and Ukrainian operations; sold Argentinian assets 2014 and consolidated into pure-play Ukrainian operator via merger with Harmelia (2013, brought 40,000 ha extra). Land bank peaked ~120,000 ha in 2014; reduced to ~28,500 ha by 2020 via lease non-renewals and disposals to deleverage. Multiple debt restructurings 2014-2016 and equity recap 2023. Operating expense breakdown (Cost of sales / Administrative expenses) drawn from consolidated income statement of AgroGeneration annual reports filed on agrogeneration.com IR archive; H1 communiqu\u00e9s disclose revenue only with no EBITDA or expense split, so field omitted on H periods.",
